            <profile id="3f95-a92e-0a43-2fa3" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword. May have light armour (+3 pts), shield (+2 pts), large shield (+3 pts, only if on foot), javelins (+2 pts), throwing spear (+2 pts). May be mounted on a horse (+8 pts). May be Drilled (+2 pts). May be Stubborn (+3 pts). If no other Army General is chosen, one Sayyid may be made Army General (+25 pts). (El Cid p.50)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="9e14-9f0d-1886-1410" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="6+">
