            </profile>
            <profile id="b16b-c5c7-6609-f29b" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Sword. May have light armour (+3 pts). May be Drilled (+2 pts). May be Stubborn (+3 pts). The Imam may lead a unit of either Black Guard or Berber Spearmen (with or without Berber Archers); he cannot lead any other unit. The Imam is subject to Hatred of the enemy, as is any unit he leads. 0-1. The army may not include an Imam if a Christian Captain is the Army General. (El Cid p.50)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="e660-3885-9248-da92" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
              <modifiers>
                <!-- armour-save -->
              <modifier type="set" field="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1" value="6+">
                <conditions>
                <condition field="selections" scope="43b4-24f2-eb57-58e7" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" childId="a695-275e-deef-cd8c" type="atLeast"/>
                </conditions>
              </modifier>
              </modifiers>
            </profile>
