  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="9492-3445-0e35-7c64" name="African Invaders (El Cid) - List Notes" publicationId="2127-dab1-0af6-7421" hidden="false">
      <description>THE AFRICAN INVADERS ARMY LIST (El Cid, pp.43-51): the Almoravids (c.1042-1149) and the Almohads (c.1128-1269). Percentages are by points. Special rules p.46 (African Drummers: certain units may feature two Musician models for +5 pts per model; any unit so equipped automatically wins a drawn combat by one point; a Berber Archer or combined Berber Archers/Spearmen unit with two drummers may use Massed Archery even if it has moved up to its normal movement, with the -1 to hit still applying).
Not enforced: "up to half the units of Berber Spearmen may be Stubborn" (Almohads).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Almoravids]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: Almoravids: at least 33%
  Uncommon Troops: Almoravids: up to 33%
  The Almoravids, c.1042-1149 AD (p.48). Characters up to 25% (Emir or Venerable Emir, Sayyid, Christian Captain, Army Standard Bearer, Imam; the Army General may be an Emir, Venerable Emir, Sayyid or Christian Captain). Common Troops at least 33%: Black Guard, Berber Spearmen, Berber Archers, Berber Cavalry, Tribal Skirmishers. Uncommon Troops up to 33%: Hasham Guard Cavalry, Camel Riders, Mercenary Caballeros, Crossbowmen and Knights, Ghuzz Horse Archers. Any Berber Spearmen unit may be made Stubborn (+3 pts per model). Andalusian Allies (up to 33%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers) are not built.
[Almohads]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: Almohads: at least 50%
  Uncommon Troops: Almohads: up to 50%
  The Almohads, c.1128-1269 AD (p.49). Characters up to 25% (same as the Almoravids). Common Troops: Black Guard, Berber Spearmen, Berber Archers, Berber Cavalry, Tribal Skirmishers (the book prints "up to 50%", which looks like a misprint of "at least 50%"; entered as at least 50%). Uncommon Troops up to 50%: Hasham Guard Cavalry, Camel Riders, Mercenary Caballeros, Crossbowmen, Jinetes, Spearmen, Archers and Knights, Ghuzz Horse Archers. Up to half the units of Berber Spearmen may be Stubborn (+3 pts per model); Christian Captains and Mercenary Knights may exchange spears for lances (+4 pts) and have horse barding (+2 pts). Andalusian Allies (up to 33%: Andalusian Jinetes, Noble Cavalry, Knights, Spearmen, Archers, Skirmishers, Crossbowmen, Mounted Crossbowmen) are not built.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
